+### P14 — semantic destination cold-reference correction, 6 November 2026
+
+This entry supplements the inert initial P14 qualification framework; it does
+not accept P14 or replace the earlier P12 records. The initial P14 attempt failed
+at Clippy because a new test diagnostic required Debug for ControlResponse.
+After the diagnostic-only correction, semantic-ready split attempts R2–R4
+failed. Their failed receipts remain evidence. The final bounded private failure
+export identified the native qualifier's actual error: destination semantic
+readiness was incomplete, without an underlying filesystem/model error.
+
+The production cause was a missing **installed default-model reference**.
+Source-only indexing deliberately calls `configured_model_objects(false)` and
+does not provision a default model implicitly. Binding shared-model metadata
+alone therefore yielded no configured model in the fresh destination. Its
+publication had Disabled semantics and no retained enrichment work; all 32
+bounded enrichment turns returned without making it Ready. Extending timeouts,
+changing source fairness or weakening the readiness proof would not fix that
+missing input.
+
+The narrow correction uses the existing canonical bundled-model selection owner
+for a claimed **semantic-ready DestinationBuild**, before Current initialization
+and indexing. The helper installs or reuses its paired default assets/reference;
+the selected descriptor is validated against paired metadata and persisted using
+the destination's actual owned, prepaid quota context. Shared model assets keep
+the existing service model owner's separate quota and lifetime. Lexical-only
+split, original custom-model choice, source contents, ranking/OCR dependencies
+and the 32-turn readiness bound are unchanged. A model/setup failure remains a
+failed job, not a fabricated readiness receipt.
+
+The regression explicitly verifies that `ServiceModelFiles::default_reference`
+is absent before accepting the semantic-ready split. It then requires a real
+ready destination publication, exact saved model descriptor, actual vectors and
+complete native/CLI/MCP observations. This is a **cold installed-reference**
+precondition, not a cold OS-cache or absent global asset-bytes claim. Helper
+presence/aggregate loads do not establish extra destination forward counts or
+model-cost deltas.
+
+The corrected-source debug semantic R2 case passed **1/1**, with a **39.64-second**
+test runtime (**45.513 seconds** including the command), and strict full-workspace
+all-target/all-feature Clippy passed in **2.551 seconds**. Both receipts retain
+source
+`d4e48a534881ea910bcbadd182e8fb4f6a970c844df6ab1951d7b566cbcb2eeb`
+(**960 inputs**). These are root-owned observed results, not independent reruns
+by the reviewer. The combined canonical fix received a separate static review;
+the reviewer disclosed authorship of the earlier test/diagnostic portions.
+
+This is now a production delta, so the prior compiled-source `4121692a…` runtime
+and its external-test-only class seal cannot qualify the fix. A fresh matched
+optimized producer, source-bound Neo testing with unconditional `cargo clean`,
+the cumulative suite and selected installed/resource/platform gates remain
+separate requirements. No full-suite pass, optimized result, new Neo result,
+default ONNX quality/cost, physical power-loss or installed-editor outcome is
+claimed by this entry. P14, subsequent missing-source cleanup and the final local
+installer remain incomplete until their actual evidence is collected/reviewed.
